5. Machine Learning, AI, and Text/Data Mining Prohibition

5.1 The Materials may not be used, directly or indirectly, for Machine Learning Use. For clarity, prohibited uses include using any Materials as:

(a) training, fine-tuning, reinforcement-learning, alignment, evaluation, benchmark, validation, test, or calibration data;

(b) prompts, prompt context, retrieval-augmented generation context, agent context, tool context, code-completion context, or grounding material;

(c) embeddings, vector representations, semantic indexes, feature sets, labels, annotations, synthetic datasets, summaries, abstractions, or transformed corpora;

(d) inputs to or outputs from any system intended to generate, transform, analyze, classify, explain, summarize, translate, refactor, complete, or synthesize code, text, data, models, decisions, or workflows; or

(e) material for evaluating, comparing, ranking, red-teaming, safety-testing, performance-testing, or improving any AI, ML, automated decision, coding-assistant, retrieval, or agentic system.

5.2 This prohibition applies regardless of whether the Materials are transformed, anonymized, tokenized, summarized, embedded, vectorized, sampled, partially extracted, paraphrased, or combined with other materials.

5.3 This prohibition applies to all Materials, including source code, documentation, telemetry, manifests, schemas, hashes, Merkle roots, commit history, repository structure, issues, discussions, metadata, and any Derivative Work.

5.4 The Licensor expressly reserves all rights for text and data mining, machine learning, model training, model evaluation, automated analysis, scraping, and indexing. No consent is granted for any such activity.

5.5 Nothing in this Section restricts the Licensor's own use of the Materials.

